<hr><h2> Returns analysis</h2>

<div id="clickable5" class="clickable">
  <a>
    &#8505
  </a>
</div>

<div id="content5" class="content">
    The following charts show total annualized returns over the coming month, <i> assuming an unchanged yield curve shape </i>. They will be useful to portfolio managers who wish to favour total yield carry and slide as opposed to directional or RV plays. The total returns are shown in conjunction with the instantaneous forward curve (red points) and the yield-to-maturity curve (green points). At points where total return and YTM diverge signficantly, this will be due to roll/slide effects. Note that the instantaneous forward curve is a useful barometer for where peak returns can be obtained, were the curve made up of forward zero coupon rates. If bonds do not match it perfectly, that is because of coupon effects, which are greater at longer maturities and for higher coupons. Please note that total returns are significantly impacted by possible curve moves, and reinvestment risk, neither of which is taken into account here.
</div>

